    board(qa): file CF-200 — six board rows store detail/detail.evidence as a bare string
    
    Measured at 2bb114f (174 rows, complete=59): `detail` null=29 / object=143 / string=2 (CF-128,
    CF-130); among object rows `detail.evidence` array=76 / absent=63 / string=4 (CF-172, CF-173,
    CF-174, CF-179). Any consumer written against the documented array-of-objects shape aborts on those
    rows instead of reporting them: `jq -e 'select(.id=="CF-172") | .detail.evidence[]'` exits 4
    (`Cannot iterate over string`), `select(.id=="CF-128") | .detail.evidence[]` exits 4 (`Cannot index
    string with string "evidence"`), while the same expression on CF-197 exits 0. Nothing in the tree
    can fail on this: `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`, `key uniformity: 174/174`,
    zero detail.evidence warnings. The four evidence-string rows also cite
    `~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/...`, a host path that resolves from no clone.
    
    Boundary checked by class census before filing: distinct from CF-074 and CF-144 (complete-row
    artifact resolvability, tree_fp instruments), from CF-045/CF-084 (CF-011/CF-013 cite one pruned
    absolute scratch log) and from CF-199 (the ACCEPTANCE-PLAN pin names an unpublished commit)
    because this is a TYPE-SHAPE failure on pending rows that breaks consumers before resolvability is
    reachable.
    
    Id disclosure: this row was first appended as CF-199 against tip a564cda, where the id was free.
    While that commit was being pushed the sync lane landed its own CF-199 (filed 10:22:19Z, before the
    append here) in the merges e820d05/294e9b1, so the id belonged to another finding. The abandoned
    commit is preserved as branch `qa-cf199-attempt` (f2ecad7) and the row was re-filed here as CF-200
    against the published tip, with the census re-measured at 2bb114f. A row id is not a reservation.
    
    The row carries a one-line portable probe (1229 B, extracted back out of the board and re-executed
    before this commit) with a positive control, and six acceptance criteria. The repair is future work
    tracked by the row and is not claimed here.
    
    Guard: `gitreins guard --scope staged` -> Tier 1 DEGRADED PASS rc=2, `lint — skipped (no staged
    files)` — the documented CF-031 refusal for a board-only diff. Committed with
    `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`: disclosed bypass, board bookkeeping only, no other arm skipped (secrets
    clean, tests full PASS). Gate at this tree: `tests/selftest.sh` SELFTEST: PASS;
    `scripts/boardctl validate` RESULT: OK (4 pre-existing warnings). Diff is insert-only: 1/0 per
    board file.
    
